# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads. Cloud Build does NOT read .dockerignore --
# that one only governs what the Docker daemon sees once the source has already
# been shipped. Without this file the whole ~966 MB repo went up on every deploy,
# because .gitignore does not cover video-studio/ (627M) or output/ (168M).
#
# Deliberately a blocklist. .gcloudignore uses gitignore semantics, where a file
# inside an excluded directory cannot be re-included -- so the `*` + `!keep-this`
# allowlist used in .dockerignore would silently drop scripts/ and break the
# build. Safer to name the heavy things.

.git/
.gcloudignore

# Secrets and credentials must never reach a build log. Note the .bak variants:
# `*token*.json` does NOT match `drive-token.json.bak`, and that file is real and
# present in this repo -- it was verified as uploading before these lines existed.
.env
.env*
*token*
*-key.json
*credential*
oauth-client.json
*.json.bak
*.bak

# Generated assets and local working files. None are COPYed by either Dockerfile.
video-studio/
output/
screenshots/
screenshots_import_output/
interactives/
references/
archives/
reports/
audits/
context/
decisions/
templates/
.claude/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
